{"created": "2024-09-18T06:54:32.289803+00:00", "modified": "2025-10-14T08:12:40.807004+00:00", "id": 13759492, "conceptrecid": "13759491", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13759492", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.13759491", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13759492", "metadata": {"title": "SynthSOD: Developing an Heterogeneous Dataset for Orchestra Music Source Separation", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13759492", "publication_date": "2024-09-13", "description": "<p>The SynthSOD dataset contains more than 47 hours of multitrack music obtained by synthesizing orchestra and ensemble pieces from the <a href=\"https://qsdfo.github.io/LOP/database.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Symbolic Orchestral Database (SOD)</a> using Spitfire BBC Symphony Orchestra Professional Library. To synthesize the MIDI files from the SOD, we needed to fix the original files into the General MIDI standard, select a subsect of files that fitted into our requirements (e.g.,&nbsp; containing only instruments that we could synthesize), and develop a new system to generate musically-motivated random annotations about tempo, dynamic, and articulation. The code to replicate this process is available in <a href=\"https://github.com/repertorium/HQ-SOD-generator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our repository</a> and all the details can be read in <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1109/OJSP.2025.3528361\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our paper</a>. We have also published the code to train and evaluate the baseline and the pre-trained models in a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/repertorium/SynthSOD-Baseline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub repository</a>.</p>\n<p>We have also published the aligned score information for most of the pieces <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14971533\">here</a>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Garcia-Martinez, Jaime", "affiliation": "Universidad de Ja\u00e9n", "orcid": "0009-0006-6407-1694"}, {"name": "Diaz-Guerra, David", "affiliation": "Tampere University", "orcid": "0000-0002-1041-0498"}, {"name": "Politis, Archontis", "affiliation": "Tampere University", "orcid": "0000-0002-0595-2356"}, {"name": "Virtanen, Tuomas", "affiliation": "Tampere University", "orcid": "0000-0002-4604-9729"}, {"name": "Carabias-Orti, Julio J.", "affiliation": "Universidad de Ja\u00e9n", "orcid": "0000-0002-6296-1101"}, {"name": "Vera-Candeas, Pedro", "affiliation": "Universidad de Ja\u00e9n", "orcid": "0000-0003-0866-703X"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1109/OJSP.2025.3528361", "relation": "isDescribedBy", "resource_type": "publication-journal", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.14971533", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}], "references": ["J. Garcia-Martinez, D. Diaz-Guerra, A. Politis, T. Virtanen, J. J. Carabias-Orti and P. Vera-Candeas, \"SynthSOD: Developing an Heterogeneous Dataset for Orchestra Music Source Separation,\" in IEEE Open Journal of Signal Processing, vol. 6, pp. 129-137, 2025, doi: 10.1109/OJSP.2025.3528361"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1109/OJSP.2025.3528361"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-sa-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "101095065", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100000780::101095065", "funder": {"name": "European Commission", "doi": "10.13039/501100000780", "acronym": "EC"}, "title": "Researching and Encouraging the Promulgation of European Repertory through Technologies Operating on Records Interrelated Utilising Machines", "acronym": "REPERTORIUM", "program": "HORIZON.2.2", "url": "https://cordis.europa.eu/projects/101095065", "doi": "10.3030/101095065"}], "communities": [{"id": "repertorium"}, {"id": "eu"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "13759491"}}]}}, "title": "SynthSOD: Developing an Heterogeneous Dataset for Orchestra Music Source Separation", "links": {"self": "https: